What is the difference between a while and do-while loop?илактиassistant

The main difference between a while and do-while loop is that the condition for the while loop is checked before the body of the loop is executed, while the condition for the do-while loop is checked after the body of the loop has already been executed at least once. This means that the do-while loop will always execute its body at least once, while the while loop might never execute its body if the initial condition is false. Additionally, while loops are often used for counting or looping through collections, whereas do-while loops are more commonly used for validating input or ensuring a desired state has been reached.assistant

